= As We May Think / 诚如所思

#html.p(id: "en-G001")[#text("Bush imagines a personal device for keeping documents and following connections between them. The problem is how accumulated knowledge can remain usable for a working mind.")]

#zh(id: "G001")[#text("布什设想一种个人设备，用来保存资料，并沿着资料之间的联系阅读。问题在于：不断积累的知识，怎样才能持续为思考所用？")]

#html.p(id: "en-G002")[#text("Memex combines storage, retrieval, annotation, and associative trails. Its proposed machinery belongs to its era, while the emphasis on connecting information remains recognizable.")]

#zh(id: "G002")[#text("Memex 把存储、检索、批注和联想路径结合起来。设想中的机械装置属于它的时代，而把信息连接起来的思路，今天读来仍很熟悉。")]

#html.p(id: "en-G003")[#text("The essay is especially relevant to a personal reading collection: saving an article is only one step. Recording why it connects to another article can preserve a line of thought.")]

#zh(id: "G003")[#text("这篇文章特别适合个人阅读收藏：保存文章只是一步。记录它为什么与另一篇文章相连，才能保存一条思考的线索。")]

#html.p(id: "en-G004")[#text("Reading question: which relationships would you want your own archive to remember? Compare a collection organized by folders with one organized around questions and connections.")]

#zh(id: "G004")[#text("阅读时可以追问：你希望自己的资料库记住哪些关系？试着比较按文件夹整理的收藏，与围绕问题和联系组织的收藏。")]
